शक, अस्, m., N. of a king (especially applied to
Śāli-vāhana); an era, epoch (especially that of the
monarch Śāli-vāhana, commencing seventy-eight
years after the Christian; cf. शाक); N. of a country;
of a particular tribe or race of people, (usually आस्, pl.;
in the legends which relate the contests between
Vasiṣṭha and Viśvā-mitra the Śakas are fabled to
have been produced by the Cow of Vasiṣṭha, from
her sweat, for the destruction of Viśvā-mitra's army;
in Manu

शक्वन्, आ, अरी, अ, Ved. powerful, able, mighty;
(आ), m. an elephant; (अरी), f. a kind of river, &c.
See under शक्वर below.

शक्कर शक्कर, अस्, m. (= शक्वर), a bull;
(ई), f. a river; a zone, girdle; a particular kind of
metre (= शक्वरी, q. v.); a woman of impure caste.

शाकुनिक, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to birds, belonging
to omens, ominous; (अस्), m. a fowler, bird-catcher;
(अम्), n. interpretation of omens or dreams, &c.

शाकुनेय, अस्, ई, अम्, relating to birds or omens;
(अस्), m. a small owl (= डुण्डुल); N. of a Muni,
(शाकुनेया धर्माः, the laws of Śākuneya.)

सकैतव स-कैतव, अस्, आ, अम्, having fraud,
fraudulent; (अस्), m. a deceiver, cheat, impostor;
(अम्), ind. fraudulently.
